      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOT DIGITY BOOM (4) is in good order and looks well placed after finishing second in a CL6 at Townsville. His previous BM70 third was a nose defeat, so the consistency is strong, and the drop from 61kg to 55kg is a major advantage. ARCTIC BEAR (6) is a genuine danger after a close CL6 second at this venue two back before making ground from too far back at Townsville, with last week's trial keeping him ticking over. TURN BIRD (3) had excuses when fourth over 1000m last week and his nose second two starts ago reads well enough to put him in the winning conversation. SPIRIT MEISTER (1) rises from a picnic win at Atherton, but his outstanding record at this track and distance gives him a solid platform to run well again. IMPARDOO (2) has built nicely into this campaign and should be at his top now on the quick back-up. Worth including.",
